ormulas to AC26. Bibliographic identity: Identical authors/title/year and original manuscript URL; same attached 108-page edition. This is the same reading event, with no additional independent credit. Exact attached 108-page edition SHA256 283bba102dd1d5dc346af81b28145bdaaea6654398d5032e76e97bafb9a858f2: section10.5 and Lemma10.7 p.90; rational component count and bielliptic product p.91; section10.6 starts p.94. Scope: Opened printed pp.90-93, including the actual coinvariant map, pair sequence, rank formula and stated hypotheses of the bielliptic example. The section10.6 heading was located on p.94; no complete section10.6 reading is claimed by this record. Bibliographic identity: Identical authors/title/year and original manuscript URL; same attached 108-page edition. This is the same reading event, with no additional independent credit. Original supplied manuscript: Remark1.2 p4 and Remark9.26 p83. Scope: Read the two exact remarks repeating the HKP Corollary1.3 bound and their stated scope. Only this comparison with the universal vector-field bound is recorded here; it is separate from the parent’s other AC26 source readings. Bibliographic identity: Identical authors/title/year and original manuscript URL; same attached 108-page edition. This is the same reading event, with no additional independent credit. Attached original108-page manuscript: Proposition9.24 with full proof pp82–83; full Remarks9.25–9.26 p83. Scope: Read the original PDF text and visually inspected both printed pages82–83. Opened the complete Proposition9.24 proof: actual etale quotient, reference-fan cocharacter, full fixed P1, and weights+1,−1. Read the complete finite-subgroup fixed-lattice criterion in Remark9.25 and the alternative two-point computation in Remark9.26. These establish the credited original reference-fan scope. The full arbitrary-basis fan classification, periodic flops and all-fan cap-freeness application are independently proved in the receiving F35. No entire-source or